        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">For most homes, a treadmill is the most versatile cardio
            machine</strong> — it walks, climbs and runs, and needs no skill. A bike, rower or
            elliptical is the better choice when impact, noise or space decide it, and a walking
            pad suits easy walking around work.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose by goal first, then joints, space and neighbours, then budget, and use the
            <a href="/treadmill-vs-elliptical/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">head-to-head comparisons</a>
            to settle the last two contenders. If you have a health condition,
            <strong class="text-white">ask your clinician before you buy</strong>.
          </p>
